#!ipxe
# Built into our iPXE: get an address, then fetch the boot menu from the PXE server over TFTP.
# The server's address comes from its proxy DHCP reply, so nothing here is fixed. When the menu
# finishes (start from the disk), this exits too and the firmware moves on to the disk.
:retry
dhcp || goto retry
chain tftp://${proxydhcp/dhcp-server}/boot.ipxe && exit ||
chain tftp://${next-server}/boot.ipxe && exit ||
echo Couldn't reach the UltimateTV PXE server. Starting from the disk in 10 seconds.
sleep 10
exit
